    },
    {
      "content": "Martin weighs \\(57\\) kg.\n\nCarl weighs:\n\\[\n57+18=75\\text{ kg}\n\\]\n\nLet the other two men weigh \\(x\\) kg and \\(y\\) kg. Then the average weight is:\n\\[\n\\frac{57+75+x+y}{4}\n=\\frac{132+x+y}{4}\n\\]\n\nSince the weights of the other two men are not given, the average cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Insufficient information}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
